## LEGACY-RME-PDF-1B — upload runtime, queue and page rendering

21. Legacy archive bytes live on the **dedicated private disk**
    `legacy_rme_private`, rooted **outside** the `local` disk root and with
    `serve` disabled. Laravel registers a `storage.{disk}` route for a local disk
    with `serve => true`, so anything under that root is in principle addressable
    by a signed framework URL — clinical archive pages must not be.
    `LegacyRmeStorageService::assertPrivateDisk()` refuses a configured disk that
    is forbidden, public, carries a `url`, or has `serve` enabled.
22. Storage paths are **opaque**: an integer surrogate key plus a
    server-generated UUID. Never a patient name, KTP/NIK, phone, address,
    diagnosis, doctor name or the uploaded filename. The original filename is a
    display label only — sanitized, bounded, and never used to build a path.
23. **PDF processing never happens in an HTTP request.** Only the queued
    `ProcessLegacyRmePdfImport` rasterizes, on its own `legacy-rme-documents`
    queue, carrying only the import id — never a model and never bytes.
24. Every binary invocation goes through `LegacyRmeProcessRunner` as an
    **argument array** with an explicit timeout. Never an interpolated shell
    string, never a caller-supplied binary path. Process diagnostics (stderr,
    command line) go to the log only — never onto the exception, which is both
    rendered and persisted to `failure_message`.
25. A PDF is validated from its **own bytes**: detected MIME, the `%PDF-` magic,
    the size limit, then a structural `pdfinfo` parse. Never the extension and
    never the client-declared Content-Type. Encrypted and password-protected
    PDFs are refused, as are documents over the page/dimension/pixel limits.
26. The source SHA-256 is computed **server-side**; a client-supplied checksum is
    never an input. Exact-file duplicates are refused for a published record and
    for an in-flight staging row, and a FAILED same-patient duplicate is pointed
    at Retry instead of creating a second staging row. A **VOID** record never
    blocks — 1A defines correction as "VOID plus a fresh import", so blocking
    there would break the documented path. A FAILED/CANCELLED row for a
    *different* patient never blocks either — that is the mis-assignment fix.
27. Processing is **idempotent and retry-safe**: the status claim is one locked
    transaction, stale output and stale page rows are cleared before rendering,
    and pages upsert on `UNIQUE(legacy_import_id, page_number)`. The temporary
    render directory is always removed, including on failure.
28. Every failure lands the import in `FAILED` with a **stable code** from
    `LegacyRmePdfFailure` and a safe message. Branch on the code, never the
    message. `failure_message` never contains a path, a command line or a stack
    trace.
29. Retry is only legal from `FAILED` (or a stale `PROCESSING`). There is no
    `READY_FOR_REVIEW → QUEUED` edge and this sprint does not invent one, nor
    abuse `FAILED` to fake it — a rendered document is corrected by cancelling
    and re-uploading.
30. The furthest a document goes in 1B is **`READY_FOR_REVIEW`**. No review
    approval, no publish, no promotion into `trx_rme_legacy_records`, no
    timeline, no doctor viewer, no annotation, no OCR. There is **no publish
    route**.
31. Private files are served only by the policy-gated streaming route, which
    resolves the import through the repository with the caller's scope
    (out-of-scope is a **404**, not a 403, so ids cannot be probed) and looks a
    page up **through** its import so a page number cannot cross imports.
    Responses carry an explicit Content-Type, `nosniff` and
    `Cache-Control: private, no-store`, and echo back neither the storage path
    nor the original filename.
32. The archive routes are **not** nested under another module's permission
    group: the five 1A permissions are the boundary. Three independent gates
    apply on every action — route `permission:` middleware, the feature-flag
    check (disabled ⇒ **404**), and the policy.
33. Thumbnails are produced by **Poppler `-scale-to`**, not a PHP image
    extension, so rendering behaves identically on every environment (the local
    dev machine has no GD). They are PNG. Page images are validated with
    `getimagesize()`, which is core and needs no extension. `pdftoppm` zero-pads
    its numeric suffix to the page-count width, so output is always discovered by
    scanning the directory and parsing the suffix — never by assuming a filename.
34. Selecting a patient by surrogate key must not be a weaker door than the
    canonical Nomor-RM search that produced the link: it goes through
    `LegacyRmePatientLookupService::findSelectable()`, which applies the same
    doctor patient scope, on both the create screen and the store action.
35. `poppler-utils` (`pdfinfo`, `pdftoppm`) is a runtime dependency of any host
    that processes documents. Tests use deterministic fakes; the one real-Poppler
    suite **skips** when the binaries are absent — it never silently passes.

## LEGACY-RME-PDF-1C — controlled publish and patient history

36. A staged import becomes an archive only through **REVIEW then PUBLISH**. The
    1A transition map is the contract and is never widened: `READY_FOR_REVIEW →
    REVIEWED` (permission `review_legacy_rme_imports`) and `REVIEWED →
    PUBLISHED` (permission `publish_legacy_rme_imports`). `PUBLISHED` is
    terminal — there is no republish and no `PUBLISHED → PROCESSING` edge.
37. **A policy is not a boundary for Super Admin.** The single global
    `Gate::before` grants Super Admin every ability, and Super Admin is the only
    role holding the legacy permissions — so every rule that must actually hold
    is enforced again in the service (status, date, pages, source file) or the
    controller (VOID streaming, feature flag). Tests assert each one *as a Super
    Admin*, not only as a permission holder.
38. Publishing runs in **one `DB::transaction` opened with `lockForUpdate`** on
    the staging row, re-reads its status under that lock, and is idempotent: an
    existing record for the `source_import_id` short-circuits to that record.
    `UNIQUE(source_import_id)` on `trx_rme_legacy_records` is the independent
    database-level defence behind it. A disabled button is never the protection.
39. The 1A date rules are **re-validated at publish time** against a freshly
    resolved cutoff. `earliest_native_rme_date_snapshot` is evidence of what was
    checked at intake, never the authority for a permanent record.
40. Publishing **promotes metadata and moves no bytes**. 1B already wrote the
    source PDF and the rendered pages into an opaque, private, per-import
    directory that is never rewritten. Nothing is copied, so a rolled-back
    publish cannot orphan a file and a retry cannot duplicate one.
41. Publishing refuses an incomplete archive with a stable, path-free code:
    `RENDERED_PAGES_MISSING`, `PAGE_COUNT_MISMATCH`, `PAGE_FILE_MISSING`,
    `SOURCE_FILE_MISSING`, `IMPORT_NOT_PUBLISHABLE`, `IMPORT_NOT_REVIEWABLE`.
    Fewer rendered pages than the document declares would silently truncate a
    clinical record and is always refused.
42. **A refusal is audited AFTER the transaction unwinds.** An audit row written
    inside the failing transaction is rolled back with it and the trail vanishes.
    `LegacyRmePublishRefusal` carries the field and the PII-free metadata out of
    the transaction, and is converted to a `ValidationException` at the boundary
    — the internal refusal type never escapes as a 500.
43. A published legacy record is **immutable**: no update route, no delete route,
    no republish route, and `LegacyRmeRecordPolicy::update`/`delete` are
    hard-wired `false`. The only correction is VOID plus a fresh import.
44. **Only PUBLISHED records reach the patient's history.** Staged, failed,
    cancelled and VOIDed rows are work in progress or retracted evidence and
    never appear there.
45. Legacy and native RME stay **separate domain entities**. Publishing creates
    no `ClinicVisit`, `MedicalRecord`, invoice, payment, consent, odontogram, lab
    candidate/order or SATUSEHAT candidate, and never changes a visit status. The
    merged timeline is a presentation projection only.
46. The timeline is ordered by the **clinical** date (`rme_date` for legacy,
    `visit_date` for native), never by upload or creation time, with a
    deterministic tie-break. Legacy rows are visually distinct from native rows.
    With the flag off, without the permission, or with no archive, the merged
    card renders nothing at all.
47. A **VOIDed archive stops streaming its bytes** (404, enforced in the
    controller so `Gate::before` cannot bypass it). VOID exists for a mis-filed
    archive — canonically one attached to the WRONG patient — so serving those
    bytes on would keep serving the leak the void retracted. The row itself stays
    readable: retracted, not erased.
48. `LegacyRmeImportPageStatus::VIEWABLE` is deliberately wider than
    `PUBLISHABLE`: a published import's pages become `PUBLISHED` and the staging
    screen — the operator's evidence of what was reviewed — must stay readable.
    Publishing stays `READY`-only.
49. Streaming honours the **disk stored on the row** (`diskFor()`, which
    re-asserts the disk is private) rather than whatever the config points at
    today, so repointing the configured disk cannot silently 404 history.
50. Review is a mandatory **state** gate, not a second-person control:
    `publish()` deliberately does not require a different actor than
    `reviewed_by`, because only Super Admin currently holds either permission. If
    four-eyes becomes a requirement, enforce it in the service and grant the two
    permissions to different roles.
51. Gallery thumbnails are **not** audited — opening an archive already writes
    `RECORD_VIEWED`, and a row per thumbnail would bury the real events. A real
    page view still writes `RECORD_PAGE_VIEWED`.
52. Production deploys keep `FEATURE_RME_LEGACY_PDF_ARCHIVE` **OFF** unless an
    explicit rollout phase authorizes enabling it. Before it is ever enabled the
    `legacy-rme-documents` queue must be served by the managed worker and
    `poppler-utils` must be present.

## LEGACY-RME-MASTERDATA-1 — patient identity and master-data integrity

53. **Identity is EXACT.** A legacy document is bound to a patient only when the
    stored Nomor RM equals the input, or the input equals a **whole manual
    segment** of a canonical Nomor RM. `LIKE '%2541'` would also hit the manual
    number `22541`, which is a different patient — a shorter number may never
    stand in for a longer one.
54. **Similarity is never identity.** Edit distance, one-digit resemblance, a
    shared branch or a shared date are INVESTIGATIVE SIGNALS. They are reported
    stamped `bindable => false` / `identity_authority => false`, and nothing —
    not a service, a controller, an operator screen or a later sprint — may
    promote one to a match. There is no fuzzy fallback anywhere in the chain.
55. **Normalization never touches significant digits.** Trimming and syntax
    normalization are allowed. Changing, dropping, adding, padding or guessing a
    digit is not.
56. **Unknown and ambiguous both fail closed.** `NOT_FOUND` is a truthful answer,
    not an error to work around; `EXACT_AMBIGUOUS` / `SEGMENT_AMBIGUOUS` are
    resolved but NOT bindable. There is no first-row-wins.
57. **Existence includes soft-deleted patients** (`withTrashed()`, as
    `PatientMedicalRecordNumberService::exists()` does). A soft-deleted row still
    owns its Nomor RM; reporting "not found" for one invites a duplicate
    registration.
58. `App\Modules\LegacyRme\Services\LegacyRmePatientResolutionAuditService` is the
    canonical answer to "which patient does this Nomor RM name?", surfaced by
    `php artisan legacy-rme:patient-resolution-audit`. It is read-only and
    changes nothing. Diagnosing an unresolvable Nomor RM with ad-hoc SQL/Tinker
    against production is not a supported path — same rule as
    LEGACY-RME-OPS-CLI-1 established for import lifecycle actions.
59. A live patient whose Nomor RM the canonical parser cannot read is a
    **master-data defect** (`ARCHIVE_BRANCH_UNRESOLVABLE`): the branch resolver
    fails closed, so they can never receive a legacy archive. It is reported, not
    auto-repaired — correcting a Nomor RM is a human action through canonical
    registration.
60. **Master-data repair and legacy migration are SEPARATE operations.** Fixing,
    correcting or creating a patient never authorises importing or publishing a
    document. A resolvable Nomor RM is a precondition for migration, never an
    approval of it.
61. A missing patient is created only through canonical human-authorised
    registration, with demographics supplied by a human. Never invent identity,
    and never create a patient so that a document has somewhere to land.
62. **Wave evidence is immutable after the fact.** A later master-data correction
    never rewrites a closed wave's reconciliation or outcome; corrections are
    recorded as NEW evidence.
63. ~~`stg_rme_legacy_imports` does not store the Nomor RM printed on the
    document.~~ **CLOSED by LEGACY-RME-SOURCE-RM-BINDING-1 — see rules 65–79.**
    The source RM is now captured as structured data and the server verifies the
    operator's patient choice against it. The wave-level symptom check (distinct
    source documents bound to the same patient) is retained as a secondary
    signal, but it is no longer the only detection available.
64. **`RM 27541` is `DOCUMENT_NOT_ELIGIBLE`** (owner determination, 2026-08-16).
    It exists in no patient row (including soft-deleted), no legacy registration
    import and no audit entry. The one-digit-away `DG-LDK2-2026-22541` is NOT it.
    Reopening requires new authoritative external evidence — a register, a signed
    amendment, an official ledger — and a fresh migration approval. Never Wave-2.

## LEGACY-RME-SOURCE-RM-BINDING-1 — source RM capture & wrong-patient prevention

65. **Every NEW legacy import must capture the Nomor RM printed on the source
    document** as structured data (`source_rm_raw` verbatim + `source_rm_normalized`
    canonical + `source_rm_resolution`). It is a first-class column, never a value
    that lives only in PDF pixels, in a filename, or in an operator's memory.
66. **The source RM is INDEPENDENT of the selected patient.** It is never
    prefilled from, auto-copied from, or defaulted to the selected patient's own
    Nomor RM — in the UI, in a form request, in a service, or in a helper. An
    assertion that agrees with the selection by construction cannot catch a wrong
    selection, which is the whole reason the field exists.
67. **The filename is never source-RM authority.** `RM Landak 4.pdf` carries no
    clinical identity. Two separate authorities: `source_pdf_sha256` identifies
    the DOCUMENT; the source RM identifies the PATIENT the document asserts.
68. **OCR is assistive only.** It may suggest; it may never silently populate an
    authoritative source RM. Human confirmation is mandatory before any value is
    treated as the document's assertion. There is no OCR → automatic binding.
69. **Normalization may repair transcription; it may never change a digit.** Only
    outer whitespace, whitespace hugging a separator, and Unicode dash variants
    are folded, and a parseable value is rebuilt through
    `PatientMedicalRecordNumberService::compose()` (the exact inverse of
    `parse()`), so the manual sequence is carried verbatim. `27541` never becomes
    `22541`, `2754`, or `027541`.
70. **Identity resolution is EXACT.** Exact stored value, or the WHOLE manual
    segment — nothing else, via
    `LegacyRmePatientResolutionAuditService::resolveIdentity()`. Fuzzy /
    Levenshtein / one-digit / prefix / suffix / "nearest in branch" matching is
    investigative diagnosis only (`resolve()`) and is **unreachable from the write
    path**. It never binds a document, at any distance, in any sprint.
71. `SOURCE_RM_REQUIRED`, `SOURCE_RM_INVALID`, `SOURCE_RM_NOT_FOUND`,
    `SOURCE_RM_AMBIGUOUS`, `SOURCE_RM_PATIENT_MISMATCH`,
    `SOURCE_RM_BRANCH_MISMATCH` and `SOURCE_RM_CAPTURE_MISSING` all **FAIL
    CLOSED**. There is no operator override, no "accept anyway", no warning tier,
    and no config switch that softens any of them.
72. **The binding gate runs FIRST**, before the date rules, branch derivation,
    wave admission, capacity, the operations gate, the file hash, the stored PDF
    and the quota reservation. A refused wrong-patient binding therefore leaves
    **no staging row, no stored file, no queued job and quota delta 0**.
73. **The gate lives in the SERVICE** (`LegacyRmeSourcePatientBindingService`),
    not in the controller, the form request, the Blade view or JavaScript. HTTP,
    a direct service call and `legacy-rme:import-admin` are the same door. The
    form request validates SHAPE only; passing it proves nothing about identity.
74. **The source RM does not decide the archive's owning branch.** FIX-ROLL2-1's
    `LegacyRmeBranchResolver` still owns that (rule 95), and the gate must not
    duplicate it — duplicating it swallows FIX-ROLL2-1's specific refusals behind
    a generic identity error. The gate only compares the branch segment the
    document ASSERTS against the patient's own. Request `branch_id` remains never
    an authority.
75. **The source RM is IMMUTABLE after staging acceptance.** No UI field, no
    update path, no CLI flag and no SQL/Tinker edit rewrites it. A correction is
    CANCEL plus a fresh import — the same rule the source PDF already follows.
76. **The binding is REVALIDATED before review, before publish and on retry**,
    against the LOCKED row. Acceptance proved it against the master data as it
    was then; publishing freezes it into permanent clinical evidence, and a
    Nomor RM can be corrected in between.
77. **CANCEL is never gated by this rule.** Every "cancel and re-import"
    instruction the domain gives is a lie if cancel is blocked by the same
    refusal that produced it. Cancel is the safety valve refusal depends on.
78. **Pre-enforcement rows are never given a manufactured source RM.** Back-
    filling `source_rm_raw` from the selected patient's Nomor RM would convert a
    derived assumption into false source evidence, claiming a human confirmation
    that never happened. Such rows stay NULL, are refused at review/publish with
    `SOURCE_RM_CAPTURE_MISSING`, and are resolved by cancel + re-import. Terminal
    rows (PUBLISHED / CANCELLED / VOID) are untouched and stay readable.
79. **A refusal never discloses whose Nomor RM it is.** No patient name, id or
    Nomor RM of the OTHER patient in the message, the response or the audit
    payload — the upload form is reachable by any `create_legacy_rme_imports`
    holder, and a helpful refusal would be a patient-enumeration oracle. Audit
    carries `source_rm_normalized` + `source_rm_resolution` + the reason code
    only. `php artisan legacy-rme:source-rm-binding-check` answers the binding
    question read-only and creates nothing.
